# A heap of famously short / deadpan academic papers — the real files, with their real
# (messy) names — organized by a tag taxonomy. This `.yo/body.yo` overlay turns the
# bare directory into an instance: it adds the `tags` tree and gives each file (a blob) its tag
# memberships as `&…:-` bookmarks (so a blob carries them). Spec: docs/annotations.
#
# Each paper is FILED by an own-line `&…:-` membership bookmark — the
# embedded model: the application lives ON the target (here a blob, via the omni overlay), and the
# engine derives "the materials under a tag" as the reverse of those forward `*` edges. The tag
# pointers are document-relative (`*: ontos: …` — `:` is this directory's root). Keys are bare; a
# messy file key is quoted.

# A tag's description is its BODY (the node's own value): `name: <text>` with the sub-tags
# in the deeper block — the schema ($defs/onto, type: variant) declares the value-plus-fields
# shape, so no `!!var` tag is needed (docs/language/vs-yaml/differences/mixtures: the shape itself is the intention).
ontos: !!<*yamlover: $defs: onto> A small taxonomy for short / deadpan papers — two axes, field and genre
  field: What the paper is about
    mathematics: Mathematics
      number-theory: Number theory — Diophantine equations, sums of powers
    physics: Physics
      quantum: Quantum mechanics and measurement
      particle: Particle physics — neutrinos and the like
    earth-science: Earth science
      seismology: Seismology — earthquakes and their statistics
    chemistry: Chemistry
    psychology: Psychology
      behavior-analysis: Applied behavior analysis
  genre: How the paper is short
    brevity: The paper is famously short
      shortest-paper: Famously the shortest paper in its journal
      one-word-answer: The title is a question; the abstract answers it in a word
      empty-body: The body of the paper is (almost) entirely blank
    humor: The paper is a joke
      deadpan: Plays it completely straight
      satire: Mocks its target
    annotation: A secondary / derivative edition of another paper

# --- the papers: each is the real file (a blob) tagged by the leaf tags it belongs to, as bare
#     `&…:-` membership bookmarks (docs/annotations) ---

"S0002-9904-1966-11654-3.pdf":
  &: ontos: field: mathematics: number-theory: -
  &: ontos: genre: brevity: shortest-paper: -
  &::yamlover:ontos:'fifth tag':-

"jaba00061-0143a.pdf":
  &: ontos: field: psychology: behavior-analysis: -
  &: ontos: genre: brevity: empty-body: -
  &: ontos: genre: humor: deadpan: -

"Chemical-Free.pdf":
  &: ontos: field: chemistry: -
  &: ontos: genre: brevity: empty-body: -
  &: ontos: genre: humor: satire: -
  &::yamlover:ontos:colors:yellow:-
  &::yamlover:ontos:'first tag':-

"1110.2832v2.pdf":
  &: ontos: field: physics: quantum: -
  &: ontos: field: physics: particle: -
  &: ontos: genre: brevity: one-word-answer: -
  &: ontos: genre: humor: deadpan: -
  &::yamlover:ontos:'fifth tag':-
  &::yamlover:ontos:colors:yellow:-
  &::yamlover:ontos:'first tag':-

"1105-2_abstract_Is the sequence of earthquake in southern California, with aftershocks removed, Poissonian.pdf":
  &: ontos: field: earth-science: seismology: -
  &: ontos: genre: brevity: one-word-answer: -
  &: ontos: genre: humor: deadpan: -
